# State Schemas

This Livebook defines complete Agent state with Zoi defaults and a cross-field
rule.

## Install Jido

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)}
])
```

## Define A State Contract

```elixir
defmodule StateSchemas.CounterState do
  def schema do
    Zoi.object(%{
      count: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0),
      minimum: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(0),
      maximum: Zoi.integer() |> Zoi.default(10)
    })
    |> Zoi.refine({__MODULE__, :within_bounds, []})
  end

  def within_bounds(%{count: count, minimum: minimum, maximum: maximum}, _opts) do
    if minimum <= count and count <= maximum do
      :ok
    else
      {:error, "count must be within the ordered bounds"}
    end
  end
end
```

Keep the schema static. The refinement uses a named module function, so the
authoring contract remains explicit.

## Define The Agent

```elixir
defmodule StateSchemas.Counter do
  use Jido.Agent, name: "state_schema_counter"

  agent do
    schema StateSchemas.CounterState.schema()
    max_state_size 32_768
  end
end
```

## Apply Defaults

```elixir
agent = StateSchemas.Counter.new!(id: "bounded-counter")
agent.state
```

The result is `%{count: 0, minimum: 0, maximum: 10}`.

## Reject An Invalid Instance

```elixir
{:error, error} =
  StateSchemas.Counter.new(
    id: "invalid-counter",
    state: %{count: 11, minimum: 0, maximum: 10}
  )

error.__struct__
```

The constructor rejects the complete state. The same schema runs for direct
commands, live candidates, checkpoints, and restore.

## Check The Size Budget

```elixir
size = :erlang.external_size(agent.state)
{:ok, _agent} = Jido.Agent.validate_instance(agent)

size
```

The size is the external term size. It is not the process heap size.

Do not store PIDs, ports, references, functions, or task handles in durable
Agent state. Put them in Plugin runtimes.

Continue with [Plugin-Owned State](plugin-state.md) and
[Portable State And Checkpoints](portable-state-and-checkpoints.md).
